<title>JAPAN: Japan govt says watching yen weakness carefully.</title>
<headline>Japan govt says watching yen weakness carefully.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Japanese government is watching the yen's weakness against the dollar carefully, chief government spokesman Seiroku Kajiyama told a news conference on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Kajiyama was commenting on currency movements which saw the dollar rising above the 120-yen level in afternoon trading in Tokyo.</p>
<p>&quot;It's not specifically a yen fall. The dollar rose against other currencies too, for example against the mark,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;But anyway we have to keep a careful watch on currency moves,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
